    {
      "question": "What background check do landlords use?",
      "answer": "Landlords evaluate applicants using tenant-screening reports. These reports are consumer reports under the Fair Credit Reporting Act. If you reject an applicant or alter lease terms because of a report, federal law requires you to supply an adverse action notice naming the screening agency."
