    {
      "question": "What does a landlord have to disclose?",
      "answer": "Federal law requires landlords renting residential property built before 1978 to disclose known lead-based paint hazards and provide the official EPA pamphlet. Other disclosures depend on state and city rules."
    },
    {
      "question": "How much security deposit can a landlord charge?",
      "answer": "Security deposit limits are established by individual state and municipal laws rather than a federal standard. You must check your state rules via the [HUD tenant rights directory](https://www.hud.gov/topics/rental_assistance/tenantrights) to confirm your limit."
    },
    {
      "question": "Do I need landlord insurance?",
      "answer": "Yes. A standard homeowners policy generally excludes coverage for properties leased out to paying tenants. Ask your insurer about landlord insurance, and require tenants to carry renters insurance."
    },
    {
      "question": "What changes for a furnished or short-term rental?",
      "answer": "Furnished and short-term rentals require keeping a complete inventory of furniture and household goods provided to guests. You must also account for local rules and taxes for short stays, and lease terms governing the utilities and maintenance split."
